      "text": "The Pantanal is one of Brazil’s best-known natural regions and the world’s largest tropical wetland. Its vast expanse of open grasslands, marshes, rivers and lakes is home to capybaras, caimans and a wide variety of birds. If you’re lucky, you may also spot a jaguar or a giant otter.",
